  <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--overview-research paragraph--view-mode--default">
                      <h3>Research Focus</h3>
      		<p>Geometric Analysis and Calculus of Variations</p><p>&nbsp;</p>
	
            </div>

	
		
							<h3>Publications</h3><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Generic scarring for minimal hypersurfaces along stable hypersurfaces (with A. Song), <em>Geom. Funct. Anal.</em> (2021), to appear, arXiv:2006.03038.<br>2.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;On the Multiplicity One Conjecture in min-max theory, <em>Ann. of Math.</em> (2) 192 (2020), no. 3, 767-820.<br>3.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Existence of hypersurfaces with prescribed mean curvature I - Generic min-max (with J. Zhu), <em>Camb. J. Math.</em> 8 (2020), no. 2, 311-362.<br>4.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Min-max minimal disks with free boundary in Riemannian manifolds, (with L. Lin and A. Sun), <em>Geom. Topol. </em>24 (2020), no. 1, 471-532.<br>5.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Min-max theory for constant mean curvature hypersurfaces, (with J. Zhu), Invent. Math. 218 (2019), no. 2, 441-490.<br>6.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Min-max theory for free boundary minimal hypersurfaces I: regularity, (with M. Li), <em>J. Differential Geom.</em>, to appear, arXiv:1611.02612.<br>7.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Curvature estimates for stable minimal hypersurfaces with free boundary, (with Q. Guang and M. Li), <em>J. Reine Angew. Math.</em> 759 (2020), 245-264.<br>8.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Entropy of closed surfaces and min-max theory, (with D. Ketover), <em>J. Differential Geom.</em> 110 (2018), no. 1, 31-71.<br>9.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Min-max hypersurface in manifold of positive Ricci curvature,<em> J. Differential Geom. </em>105 (2017), no. 2, 291-343.<br>10.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Min-max minimal hypersurface in (Mn+1, g) with Ricg &gt; 0 and 2 ≤ n ≤ 6, <em>J. Differential Geom.</em> 100 (2015), no. 1, 129-160.<br>11.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;Convexity of reduced energy and mass angular momentum inequalities, (with R. Schoen), <em>Ann. Henri Poincaré</em> 14 (2013), no. 7, 1747-1773.<br>12.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;On the existence of min-max minimal surfaces of genus g ≥ 2, <em>Commun. Contemp. Math.</em> 19 (2017), no. 4, 1750041, 36 pp.</p>
	
		
